# Stock-build baseline (before prefetch). Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (MoE, 3B active), all routed experts in RAM, 128k context,
# one slot, reads images. The reference numbers in reference/rtx3070/ were measured with this shape.
# -ncmoe 40 + -ub 4096: ub 4096 doubles prefill vs. 2048 but needs compute buffer; at 128k that only fits with all
#   experts on the CPU (nc 38 -> OOM). Costs ~1.5 t/s generation.
# KV f16: q8_0 is not faster (hybrid model, few attention layers), KLD 0.003.
# --cache-reuse has no effect here (recurrent state, the server disables it) -> prefix cache + checkpoints.
# --cache-ram 4096: the default 8192 is too tight next to ~20 GB of experts in 32 GB RAM.
# --mmproj on the CPU (--no-mmproj-offload): OOM at start on the GPU. Costs ~1 GB RAM, no VRAM.
LLAMA_ARGS=-m /path/to/models/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf --alias qwen3.6-35b-a3b -ngl 99 -ncmoe 40 -fa on -t 10 -b 4096 -ub 4096 -c 131072 -np 1 --fit off --cache-ram 4096 --mmproj /path/to/models/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-mmproj-F16.gguf --no-mmproj-offload
